      },
      "line": 395,
      "exact_line": "    \\item \\textbf{Ecosystem-Wide Trends:} We identify trends across the AI agent ecosystem relating to systems' origin, role, level of agency, capabilities, safety, and transparency (\\Cref{sec:findings})."
    },
    {
      "source_ref": {
        "path": "{{REPRODUCTION_ROOT}}\\literature\\cpu_additional_complete_route_screen_oct15_002\\agent_index_original024\\exact_original_source\\arxiv.tex",
        "bytes": 118136,
        "sha256": "14e08b25caf95617721e8949a4aa71791bb6c2a5fe0ec3b5fc8400905ae40325"
      },
      "line": 290,
      "exact_line": "Notably, we find different transparency levels among agent developers and observe that most developers share little information about safety, evaluations, and societal impacts. "
    },
    {
      "source_ref": {
        "path": "{{REPRODUCTION_ROOT}}\\literature\\cpu_additional_complete_route_screen_oct15_002\\agent_index_original024\\exact_original_source\\arxiv.tex",
        "bytes": 118136,
        "sha256": "14e08b25caf95617721e8949a4aa71791bb6c2a5fe0ec3b5fc8400905ae40325"
      },
      "line": 771,
      "exact_line": "The 2025 AI Agent Index provides verified information across 1,350 fields for 30 prominent AI agents. Beyond the specific findings detailed above, we identify \\textit{persistent limitations in reporting around ecosystemic and safety-related features of agentic systems}. This Index aims to help developers design more thorough documentation frameworks, researchers identify open questions in the ecosystem, and policymakers understand gaps in transparency that may warrant attention."
    },
    {
      "source_ref": {
        "path": "{{REPRODUCTION_ROOT}}\\literature\\cpu_additional_complete_route_screen_oct15_002\\agent_index_original024\\exact_original_source\\arxiv.tex",
        "bytes": 118136,
        "sha256": "14e08b25caf95617721e8949a4aa71791bb6c2a5fe0ec3b5fc8400905ae40325"
      },
      "line": 595,
      "exact_line": "    \\caption{For 198 out of 1350 fields, we were unable to find any information (gray). This is most common in the ``Ecosystem Interaction'' and ``Safety, Evaluation, and Impact'' categories. Non-empty information fields are 14 words long on average.}"
    },
    {
      "source_ref": {
        "path": "{{REPRODUCTION_ROOT}}\\literature\\cpu_additional_complete_route_screen_oct15_002\\agent_index_original024\\exact_original_source\\arxiv.tex",
        "bytes": 118136,
        "sha256": "14e08b25caf95617721e8949a4aa71791bb6c2a5fe0ec3b5fc8400905ae40325"
      },
      "line": 717,
      "exact_line": "    \\caption{Most safety, evaluation, and social impact related fields (133/240) have no information available. Browser agents (67/104, 64\\%) and enterprise agents (25/40, 63\\%) have the most missing fields, followed by chat agents (41/96, 43\\%).}"
    }
  ],
